From 7546564284a8d8e2d312197ce9a400e8441c1f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kitae Noh <5194831+nworkers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:27:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] container: relocate a PRX to a chosen base (`--base`,
 `relocate`)

A PRX links at zero, and allegrexrecomp lifts it there: every address in the
generated code is module-relative. A host that wants the module where a PSP
would load it (user modules start at 0x08804000) has had to translate every
address at run time. This lets the toolkit do it once, at lift time.

- `prx_relocate()` builds the loaded image (all PT_LOAD segments, BSS zeroed)
  and applies SHT_PRXRELOC at a caller-chosen base: R_MIPS_32, R_MIPS_26, and
  HI16/LO16 pairs (HI16 paired with the nearest following LO16, with the carry
  a LO16 of 0x8000 or more needs).
- `funcs` and `emit` take `--base <addr>`; with it they discover and emit from
  the relocated image. Without it nothing changes.
- `relocate <file> <base> <out>` writes the relocated image, so a host can
  load the same bytes the code was lifted from.
- Pointer seeds honour the relocation's segment indices. `ofsbase` names the
  segment the patched word lives in and `addrbase` the segment the stored
  address is relative to; both were assumed to be segment 0, so relocations
  in a second segment read the wrong word.
- The unrelocated lui+addiu immediate scan is skipped when the image is
  relocated: with the image at its base those pairs already appear through
  the relocation table, and at base 0 small immediates collide with .text.

The relocated path reuses psp_collect_exports and psp_collect_pointer_seeds
(through psp_collect_pointer_seeds_at, which reads patched words from the
relocated image and the relocation table from the file).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
